  "claim_boundary": "A matched, method-native system comparison in ONE H100 session (default V2 runner, eager, single request, 2048-token prompt, 32 output tokens). TurboQuant uses its method-required attention backend (TURBOQUANT + FlashAttention v2 on its four BF16 boundary layers) while BF16 / FP8 / RABIT use TRITON_ATTN; latency differences are therefore system-level, not quantizer-kernel-level. No throughput claim (single request), no quality claim, no generalization beyond this configuration. Exp3 / Exp4 absolute TPOT are not comparable as the same experiment (different snapshot / session).",
